  id: Semimembranosus_muscle.L
  partName: Semimembranosus_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The semimembranosus is a powerful muscle involved in extending the hip and flexing
    the knee. It plays a significant role in propulsion and stabilization of the
    hindlimb. '
  - This muscle works with other posterior thigh muscles to generate force during
    movement. It is especially important during activities requiring strength and
    endurance, such as running and jumping, contributing to efficient and controlled
    locomotion.
